    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed schedule today, significantly limiting our active roster as **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are sidelined by team off-days. Consequently, **Jackson Merrill** stands as our premier play with an elite score of 66.69. Despite facing an above-average arm in May (xERA 3.99), **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the two-hole, providing a +8% order bump and a +13% dynamic platoon edge, solidifying his role as the anchor of our production for this slate.\n\nOur remaining active starters face a difficult path against high-caliber pitching. **Drake Baldwin** (49.93) manages a marginal score largely buoyed by his leadoff position; however, he faces a daunting matchup against Yamamoto, whose 3.40 xERA drags down our offensive floor. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (47.69) and **Andy Pages** (43.18) are pushed into marginal territory by a brutal encounter with Sale (xERA 2.79). While **Kyle Tucker** typically thrives, the combination of an elite southpaw and a suboptimal eighth-spot batting order makes him a high-risk start. We have opted to bench **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Heliot Ramos** in favor of this set, as their lack of plate appearance guarantees or prohibitive splits against today\u2019s opposing starters offered a lower path to efficiency than the marginal upside of our active quartet. \n\nThe injury report remains a primary constraint, with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** both out on the IL, depriving us of the stolen base profile we desperately need to secure the category. With **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias** also unavailable or providing no contribution to today's scoring, we are effectively playing a short deck. We will monitor for any late-breaking lineup changes, but expect a volatile output given the heavy reliance on our few active hitters against top-tier arms.",
